#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532736} :activity/id #uuid "e67bdbbc-b2ac-5dc2-96db-49866bc692da" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050054 :topic/id #uuid "29ce72ae-dbea-5d83-a81d-90545461cdec" :topic/math-academy-id 6375} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532728 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5a54273-3450-5c26-84d7-383486f21cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307277}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307277} :answer-field/id #uuid "3db64a2d-0768-5ffd-ba7e-05c9f4485c48" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec22e530-554e-5020-8783-f257d54f500f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307324}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307324} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5cf4951-3613-5027-8a9a-0372890bd5d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "79079e07-e6bc-5f6a-8ed1-2ff769b8b920" :question/math-academy-id "q-334729" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $3,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3t$ | $1-3t$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -3{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(3t) &={e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(3t) &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{3t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n3t{e}^{3t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}(1-3t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =6{e}^{3t}t+{e}^{3t}(1-3t) \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(1+3t), \\\\ -3{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-3{e}^{3t}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1+3t & -3t \\\\ 3t & 1-3t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "03d5d0e2-58f6-580f-b08d-c488e5333a32" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532761}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532736 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a8db4e8-f732-5d22-9704-09e0ccf298b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos(3t)+\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532285}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532285} :answer-field/id #uuid "3247c73e-d754-5617-80f3-a0beacefea90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532515} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f84eb7c6-9806-5d01-aade-ce5ce09883c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532472}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532472} :answer-field/id #uuid "4788b925-6ee1-5536-8ffa-a6478b71d51d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "900adaef-859d-5d14-9981-202d2269e069" :question/math-academy-id "q-334626" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $2\\pm 3\\text{i}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"140px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"140px\">$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 6{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -3{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=(2+3\\text{i})t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=(2-3\\text{i})t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((2+3\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(2+3\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(2+3\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & ={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\ (2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0})+3{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & ={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\,{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 3t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{3t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{3t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t+{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\ -3{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "447659a5-783c-55e2-b7bc-7044e79e9190" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532744}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532744 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7805cc61-032d-5340-b315-43d00f9ec949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306291}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306291} :answer-field/id #uuid "5694d036-6e3a-56ea-beeb-680490a87b8c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aacf013a-2689-512b-8794-bcbacddaf843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306764}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306764} :answer-field/id #uuid "674d0fa8-85cf-5f7e-bdaa-2d7ca81bb93d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f29b7109-5c33-5046-8236-7d693dea5b92" :question/math-academy-id "q-334634" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\pm 3\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\,$ |  | $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ | $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -5{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-3\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3\\text{i}t) & ={e}^{3\\text{i}t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}\\cdot 3\\text{i}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+3{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-\\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "783d8e6f-d461-5f0b-8f11-aa192fbe52a4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532728}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532761 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52b1d7ae-e4dd-5799-9115-e6e7b1fd12ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305951}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305951} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dde19ef-9af0-5255-a3d4-655b000140c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fc7ea02-06bd-5e6c-aed2-4751d80186b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305289}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305289} :answer-field/id #uuid "893c4189-3f31-573e-94ae-26b874312a53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4bf1a0f0-bb87-5dac-ad3b-1ce93c87e2a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334733" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 12 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $2,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-3t$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1-6t$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -3 \\\\ 12 & -4\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -3{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 12{\\alpha }_{1}t & -4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(2t) &={e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(2t) &={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{2t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n2t{e}^{2t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}(1-2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =8{e}^{2t}t+{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(1+6t) \\\\ 12{\\alpha }_{1}t & =12{e}^{2t}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1+6t & -3t \\\\ 12t & 1-6t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "dc3bbe46-b9a2-5b99-9ca0-73318c047651" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532762}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532762 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "753cf168-9af8-50a8-bf6d-aec9b1e3c2e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{cos}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306266}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306266} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e34fb24-26d6-54f8-8e2c-e459754da21c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa9799e7-8c6d-5377-a47d-4e6a05e2b186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{cos}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306762}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306762} :answer-field/id #uuid "4609b934-301d-57c7-89ed-e8cdd2469bcc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307743} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f24e94e-6875-5dc6-95dc-6ad3d893da7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{sin}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305283}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305283} :answer-field/id #uuid "95f2f7b3-4e91-5fb5-bc50-5086640214d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307996} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "680c33fd-8ce1-50c7-9c3f-e14b4d6e395c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{sin}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306145}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306145} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0d0c784-8e29-5661-9d95-8147778f15de" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "14f4f5f9-2f59-5657-8bee-d1931d1011cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-335107" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & -7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "eabd75d2-306c-5778-a5d4-6908c275c489"}] :activity/title "Matrix Exponentials" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531935}]}
